################################################################################
# DNA Pipeline Rules
################################################################################

## Demux-after-align architecture:
##   1. dna_trim_and_tag: rewrite matched read names as <origid>_<XXYY>_<UMI>
##      and emit spatialdmt R1/R2 pairs or clipped smcseq Watson/Crick R1.
##      Structure-fail (_SF)
##      and whitelist-miss (_WM) reads are split off here into a separate
##      Unmatched fastq pair -- they never enter the merged BAM.
##   2. dna_biscuit_align: one biscuit align -9 → dupsifter -B (cell-aware,
##      BS-correct) → samtools sort → split BAM by CB:Z tag into bam/XXYY.bam.
##      Every CB is a real whitelist coord (no sentinel cell).
##   3. dna_biscuit_pileup: size-balanced pileup over bam/*.bam; also emits
##      per-cell .conv.tsv (CA/CC/CG/CT beta sum+cnt) pooled to
##      sample-level _totalBaseConversionRate.txt for the curated table.
##
## Unmatched track runs in parallel: dna_biscuit_align_unmatched on the
## separate fastq, mqc_unmatched_biscuit + mqc_unmatched_diagnostics surface
## the bucket as its own MultiQC entry.
##
## Replaces the original demux-before-align path which spawned ~9216 biscuit
## invocations per sample.
